  data: {
    LLM: '1. Betting begins after the hole cards are dealt. 2. The outer cards of the cross are revealed one by one, with a betting round after each. 3. The middle card (shared by both paths) is revealed last for the final betting round. 4. Hand Construction: You can use the vertical column (3 cards) + your 2 hole cards OR the horizontal row (3 cards) + your 2 hole cards. You cannot mix cards from both lines.',
    Player: '1. Betting begins after the hole cards are dealt. 2. The outer cards of the cross are revealed one by one, with a betting round after each. 3. The middle card (shared by both paths) is revealed last for the final betting round. 4. Hand Construction: You can use the vertical column (3 cards) + your 2 hole cards OR the horizontal row (3 cards) + your 2 hole cards. You cannot mix cards from both lines.',
    objective: "Form the best five-card poker hand using your two hole cards and exactly one 'path' of three community cards from the cross.",
    gameplay: '1. Betting begins after the hole cards are dealt. 2. The outer cards of the cross are revealed one by one, with a betting round after each. 3. The middle card (shared by both paths) is revealed last for the final betting round. 4. Hand Construction: You can use the vertical column (3 cards) + your 2 hole cards OR the horizontal row (3 cards) + your 2 hole cards. You cannot mix cards from both lines.',
    keyRules: [
      'Must use exactly one path (vertical OR horizontal) plus your 2 hole cards',
